Day 3 - Role Based Prompting

## Question
How can I improve my chances of getting a software developer job in 6 months?

## Normal Response
The biggest decision you need to make first is which path — Frontend (websites, React) or Backend (logic, Python, APIs). At 1–2 hours/day, trying to do both at once will slow you down. Pick one and go deep.
My recommendation for a complete beginner: Start with Frontend. You see results immediately (a webpage appears!), which keeps you motivated. HTML → CSS → JavaScript → React is a clean, well-documented path with tons of free help online.
The three things that matter most:
Consistency beats intensity. 1.5 hours every day beats 10 hours on a Saturday and nothing for a week. Protect those daily hours like a gym habit.
Projects beat tutorials. After the first month, spend more time building than watching videos. Employers want to see GitHub repos, not certificates.
Rejection is part of the process. Even strong candidates get rejected constantly. Apply early (Month 5), apply often, and treat every interview as practice.
